Jahshaka patch 0052 — PlanarReflections tells you about its active actor slots.

SOURCE patch (a header, so every consumer recompiles). EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN
`irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after pulling this. It touches a file no other
patch in the stack touches
(`Components/PlanarReflections/include/OgrePlanarReflections.h`).

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325; audit
SPECS/audits/ENGINE_WORKAROUNDS_TO_PATCHES_2026-09-15.md finding F13).
`PlanarReflections::update()` gives each active actor slot its own reflection
camera, texture and CompositorWorkspace — and each of those workspaces
instantiates its own shadow node and its own pass list. Everything in Jahshaka
that has to reach a mirror's ACTUAL passes needs those workspaces: the lamp-map
cache, which must know which workspaces hold a light fixed into a cached shadow
slot (`OgreEngine::applyShadowCache`), and the render-loop monitor, which times
every pass the frame executed. `mActiveActorData` is `protected` with no
accessor, so the engine derived a `JahPlanarReflections` from the class purely
to expose two lines — "engine API through inheritance, not a patch", with a
note that `~PlanarReflections` is not virtual so the derived type is what the
scene has to hold and delete. That is the reach-in the rule names; the two
accessors are added where they belong and the derived class is deleted.

Read-only, owns nothing, and the slots are re-assigned on every `update()`, so
a returned pointer is valid for the frame it was asked in — stated in the
doc comment.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` against the pristine pin and `git apply
--reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane worktree;
`--engine-selftest` byte-identical (`b55e2d5d…`) — a header-only addition that
no existing code calls. The behavioural gate is `mirror.*`, `planar.*` and the
lamp-cache suites (the engine now reaches the same workspaces through the base
class).

--- a/Components/PlanarReflections/include/OgrePlanarReflections.h
+++ b/Components/PlanarReflections/include/OgrePlanarReflections.h
@@ -252,6 +252,30 @@
 
         uint8 getMaxActiveActors() const { return mMaxActiveActors; }
 
+        /** The ACTIVE ACTOR SLOTS: how many the component is currently rendering
+            through, and the private CompositorWorkspace each one renders with.
+
+            `update()` assigns the closest actors to the slots and gives each slot its
+            own reflection camera, texture and workspace (an instance of
+            mWorkspaceName, so each one instantiates its own shadow node, its own
+            compositor nodes and its own pass list). Those workspaces are per-slot
+            state with no public name and no other way in, so anything that has to
+            reach a mirror's actual passes — a shadow-map cache that must know which
+            workspaces hold a light fixed into a cached slot, a frame monitor that
+            times every pass the frame executed, a debug inspector — had no choice but
+            to derive from this class to read mActiveActorData. Reading the slot's
+            workspace changes nothing and owns nothing; the slot count is <=
+            getMaxActiveActors().
+        @remarks
+            The slots are re-assigned on every update( camera, aspectRatio ), so a
+            returned pointer is valid for the frame it was asked in.
+        */
+        size_t               getNumActiveActorSlots() const { return mActiveActorData.size(); }
+        CompositorWorkspace *getActiveActorWorkspace( size_t slot ) const
+        {
+            return slot < mActiveActorData.size() ? mActiveActorData[slot].workspace : 0;
+        }
+
         /// Returns the amount of bytes that fillConstBufferData is going to fill.
         size_t getConstBufferSize() const;
 
